    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Corbin Carroll** (74.99) and **Seiya Suzuki** (72.93), our premier offensive threats against favorable matchups. **Corbin Carroll** remains our highest-ceiling asset despite facing Ryan Gusto; even with a slight reduction for the pitcher\u2019s ability to hold runners, **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s elite speed profile makes him a mandatory start in our pursuit of stolen bases. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost against JR Ritchie, capitalizing on a high-upside matchup that demands his inclusion in the two-hole. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** provide high-efficiency support, with **Vinnie Pasquantino** specifically benefiting from a 14% platoon edge against Cristian Javier, which pushes his score to a robust 68.46.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **James Wood**, who sits on the bubble with a score of 51.80. While his 0.413 xwOBA is elite, the optimizer ultimately penalized him for a brutal matchup against Zack Wheeler and the increased risk of his SB potential being neutralized by a sub-1.90s catcher pop time. This caution mirrors our approach to **Brice Turang** (53.51), who remains in the lineup despite a tough draw against Jared Jones; we are accepting his lower projected floor specifically to chase stolen base upside in a tight contest. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key contributors. **Mickey Moniak** carries a strong 66.02 score, driven largely by a 14% park factor boost against Robbie Ray, but we must monitor his confirmation to ensure he isn\u2019t being rested against the southpaw. Additionally, while **Trevor Story** (58.78) and **Zach McKinstry** (53.85) are currently slated to start, their value is partially tied to their ability to exploit specific pitcher delivery tendencies\u2014any late-scratch adjustments or weather-related disruptions in their respective venues could force a pivot to the bench depth represented by **Austin Riley** or **Travis Bazzana**.",
